                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "level": 2,
                  "html": "Kalama",
                  "align": "center",
                  "size": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "html": "Images created with Eden and Midjourney",
                  "align": "center",
                  "size": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "html": "Kalama exists within Olympus Mons, the largest volcano on Mars. The intense geothermal energy of this location is Kalama’s primary resource, used to heat and provide nutrients for developing extremophile microbial life. These microbes are capable of surviving Mars' harsh conditions, transforming volcanic minerals into usable nutrients, thus fostering a nascent ecosystem within the volcanic tunnels.",
                  "align": null,
                  "size": null
                }
              ]
            },
